WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.522
A ball and feather wait
at the same height.

2
00:00:02.522 --> 00:00:05.278
In ordinary air, which
reaches the floor first?

3
00:00:05.278 --> 00:00:07.624
Make a prediction,
but also predict why.

4
00:00:07.624 --> 00:00:11.261
We will change the air without
changing the objects, height or

5
00:00:11.261 --> 00:00:12.023
release time.

6
00:00:12.023 --> 00:00:12.482
Release.

7
00:00:12.482 --> 00:00:15.124
The ball lands first
while the feather drifts.

8
00:00:15.124 --> 00:00:18.627
That observation is real, but
it does not prove gravity pulls

9
00:00:18.627 --> 00:00:19.603
only on the ball.

10
00:00:19.603 --> 00:00:22.188
Another interaction is
affecting the feather.

11
00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.370
Watch the air bend
and flow around it.

12
00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:27.829
Seal both objects inside a clear
chamber and remove almost all

13
00:00:27.829 --> 00:00:29.335
the air, creating a vacuum.

14
00:00:29.335 --> 00:00:31.901
The starting height and
release stay the same.

15
00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:34.635
If gravity needs air,
neither object should fall.

16
00:00:34.635 --> 00:00:37.368
If air caused the difference,
what should happen?

17
00:00:53.533 --> 00:00:56.897
Gravity is Earth's pull on each
object without direct contact.

18
00:00:56.897 --> 00:01:00.098
Draw a violet Earth on ball
arrow downward on the ball, and

19
00:01:00.098 --> 00:01:02.322
Earth on feather
downward on the feather.

20
00:01:02.322 --> 00:01:05.523
Both arrows remain whether the
chamber contains air or not.

21
00:01:05.523 --> 00:01:08.585
In open air, moving air particles
touch the falling objects.

22
00:01:08.585 --> 00:01:11.137
Air resistance acts against
their downward motion.

23
00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:14.301
Its effect is much more noticeable
on the wide, light feather,

24
00:01:14.301 --> 00:01:17.209
so the feather falls more
slowly even while gravity still

25
00:01:17.209 --> 00:01:18.128
pulls it downward.

26
00:01:18.128 --> 00:01:19.463
Release them in the vacuum.

27
00:01:19.463 --> 00:01:21.885
Ball and feather fall
together and land together.

28
00:01:21.885 --> 00:01:24.406
Gravity did not disappear
when the air was removed.

29
00:01:24.406 --> 00:01:27.223
Removing most air resistance
removed the large difference

30
00:01:27.223 --> 00:01:28.311
between their motions.

31
00:01:28.311 --> 00:01:30.733
Hold that result and
compare both landing frames.

32
00:01:46.897 --> 00:01:47.853
Zoom out to Earth.

33
00:01:47.853 --> 00:01:51.040
Objects above Australia, Africa
and the Pacific each have an

34
00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:53.908
Earth-on-object arrow pointing
towards Earth's centre.

35
00:01:53.908 --> 00:01:57.148
Down means towards the ground
beneath you because Earth pulls

36
00:01:57.148 --> 00:01:59.432
objects towards its
centre from every side.

37
00:01:59.432 --> 00:02:02.499
A strong comparison uses the
same ball, feather, chamber,

38
00:02:02.499 --> 00:02:04.328
starting heights
and release time.

39
00:02:04.328 --> 00:02:06.480
The air condition is
the planned change.

40
00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.707
Compare landing times, repeat
the drops, and do not secretly

41
00:02:09.707 --> 00:02:11.967
change the feather's
shape between trials.

42
00:02:11.967 --> 00:02:15.537
A helium balloon can rise, yet
Earth still pulls it downward.

43
00:02:15.537 --> 00:02:18.872
The surrounding air pushes
upward strongly enough for the

44
00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.043
motion to be upward.

45
00:02:20.043 --> 00:02:23.378
Rising or floating describes
the motion; it does not mean

46
00:02:23.378 --> 00:02:24.841
gravity has switched off.

47
00:02:41.006 --> 00:02:43.408
Someone claims gravity
needs air to work.

48
00:02:43.408 --> 00:02:46.629
The vacuum result rejects
that idea: with almost no air

49
00:02:46.629 --> 00:02:49.851
resistance, both objects
still speed downward and land.

50
00:02:49.851 --> 00:02:53.366
The changed air condition
affected their difference, not the

51
00:02:53.366 --> 00:02:54.889
existence of Earth's pull.

52
00:02:54.889 --> 00:02:55.930
Use two questions.

53
00:02:55.930 --> 00:02:57.550
Is Earth pulling the object?

54
00:02:57.550 --> 00:02:59.054
Yes, near Earth's surface.

55
00:02:59.054 --> 00:03:01.194
Is air resistance
affecting its fall?

56
00:03:01.194 --> 00:03:03.507
Only when air touches
the moving object.

57
00:03:03.507 --> 00:03:07.094
Keeping
these interactions separate explains both the open-air

58
00:03:07.094 --> 00:03:08.771
result and the vacuum result.

59
00:03:08.771 --> 00:03:12.924
A flat sheet and a tightly
crumpled sheet use the same paper.

60
00:03:12.924 --> 00:03:15.716
In air, the flat sheet
falls more slowly.

61
00:03:15.716 --> 00:03:19.733
In a vacuum, what should change,
and which force remains on

62
00:03:19.733 --> 00:03:20.550
both sheets?

63
00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:23.750
Use the two-force model
to justify your answer.
